    "rationale": "The exhaustive optimizer-free V5 audit completed all 11968 cases but failed 7386 required-safety cases, including 6985 hard impacts. Reset-pose diagnosis localized the dominant mechanism to final heel-to-forefoot height difference: impact incidence rose monotonically from about fifteen percent below 0.2 millimetres to more than eighty percent above 5.7 millimetres, and the lower foot was the selected support in about ninety-two percent of failures. V5 joint inspection then showed that the provisional ankle-only leveling path saturated the declared minus-twenty-degree ankle-pitch boundary in ninety to one hundred percent of support frames for the worst start clip, while hip-pitch and knee retained usable declared range. This new algorithm identity preserves every V5 source, crop, split, contact, timing, root, BodySchema, USD, PD, safety and gate threshold, including the full fifteen-degree ankle-roll and twenty-degree ankle-pitch hard reserves. After the V5 coupled stance solve and temporal smoothing, it adds a deterministic bilateral reset-pose closure over hip-pitch, knee and ankle-pitch for every admitted frame. Four bounded finite-difference projection iterations distribute heel-to-forefoot pitch residual across available sagittal-chain range instead of crossing an ankle reserve boundary; thirty-two symmetric smoothing passes and the existing twenty-five-percent joint-velocity projection bound the resulting trajectory before final planar-root closure. The operation targets only the diagnosed geometric input defect and does not authorize an optimizer run. Fresh deterministic import, native pose, visual-overlay and exhaustive dynamic evidence remain mandatory before TRAIN-4 can advance."
